// src/lib/solitaire-duel/puzzleCalibrationData.ts
//
// GENERATED by scripts/calibrate-puzzle-library.mjs — do not hand-edit.
//
// This is the RECORDED-HUMAN calibration snapshot for the strategic puzzle
// library. Only Beginner and Intermediate positions are eligible: they are the
// learning tiers, so a measured solve rate should be allowed to move a puzzle
// between them when the structural score got the audience wrong.
//
// An empty map is a real, honest result: when the snapshot was generated the
// database held ZERO ranked human sessions and no human attempts on any
// library puzzle, so no position had the minimum sample needed to move. The
// library therefore keeps its measured STRUCTURAL bands (see
// puzzleLibrary.ts) until recorded play exists.
//
// Each entry is `{ attempts, solves, rate, band }`:
//   * attempts — human seats that reached the position and made at least one move;
//   * solves   — human seats that advanced past it;
//   * rate     — solves / attempts, rounded to three decimals;
//   * band     — the calibrated difficulty band to use (1 or 2).
// A position whose measured rate matches its structural band is absent: only
// changes are stored, so the diff stays reviewable.

